  "body": "## What changed\n\nBox stock with retained cut history now preserves machined walls and cavities through side-on quarter turns.\nThe carry retains swept-tool geometry and reads separate material intervals along the new columns.\nLater cuts, stock clips, and further turns keep those intervals.\nFixture checks use the intervals on columns and between columns.\nA fixture can contact a finished wall or occupy a cavity without a false collision.\nThe verdict still detects a later cut through the part.\n\nThe change starts from upstream/main `6f8b309d`.\nEffort: max (not escalated).\nNo process files change.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe old carry knew column heights but lost the wall position between column centres.\nIt extended a turned face to the next empty centre and filled cavities between the outer faces.\nThe pins reproduced a 6.5 mm wall instead of 6.2 mm.\nThe pocket floor became 6 mm instead of 2 mm.\nA fixture in contact with the wall falsely penetrated it by 0.3 mm.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll 40 targeted tests pass.\nThey cover the reported failures, all 16 side turns, translations, sub-cell cavities, later cuts, clips, tool profiles, and named refusals.\nThe three critical pins failed on unchanged product code before the fix:\n\n- `a_contoured_wall_keeps_its_off_grid_position_after_a_side_turn`\n- `a_pocket_remains_cut_after_a_side_turn_and_return`\n- `a_fixture_touching_the_turned_machined_wall_is_contact`\n\nAll 18 mutations failed their named runtime test.\nEvery test passed after the fixed source was restored.\nNo mutation result relies on a compile failure.\nThe first three mutations replaced `cut.rs` with the copy from upstream/main.\nThe other mutations removed or changed one guard or safety branch.\n\n| Mutation | Pin | Mutated / restored |\n|---|---|---|\n| Original cut history: wall | `a_contoured_wall_keeps_its_off_grid_position_after_a_side_turn` | red / green |\n| Original cut history: cavity | `a_pocket_remains_cut_after_a_side_turn_and_return` | red / green |\n| Original cut history: fixture | `a_fixture_touching_the_turned_machined_wall_is_contact` | red / green |\n| Finite stock bounds | `exact_side_carry_refuses_non_finite_stock_floors_by_name` | red / green |\n| Axis size limit | `exact_side_carry_refuses_a_lattice_that_is_too_tall` | red / green |\n| Read budget | `exact_side_carry_refuses_an_excessive_read_before_building_the_lattice` | red / green |\n| Column index | `an_exact_material_read_refuses_an_out_of_range_column` | red / green |\n| Flank overflow | `exact_carry_refuses_flank_overflow_without_changing_stock` | red / green |\n| Squared radius overflow | `exact_carry_refuses_radius_squared_overflow_without_changing_stock` | red / green |\n| Chord length overflow | `exact_carry_refuses_chord_length_overflow_without_changing_stock` | red / green |\n| Cut ray budget | `exact_side_carry_refuses_a_ray_with_too_many_retained_cuts` | red / green |\n| Unbounded ray | `stock_sim::carry_history::tests::an_unbounded_exact_ray_is_refused_by_name` | red / green |\n| Clip ray budget | `stock_sim::carry_history::tests::too_many_clip_reads_refuse_the_ray_by_name` | red / green |\n| Subdivision budget | `stock_sim::carry_history::tests::exhausted_subdivision_budget_refuses_the_ray_by_name` | red / green |\n| Non-finite tool floor | `stock_sim::carry_history::tests::a_non_finite_original_axis_tool_floor_is_refused_by_name` | red / green |\n| Non-finite tool distance | `stock_sim::carry_history::tests::a_non_finite_tool_distance_is_refused_by_name` | red / green |\n| Convex endpoint proof | `stock_sim::carry_history::tests::a_convex_sweep_removes_the_segment_between_surface_endpoints` | red / green |\n| Entry material snapshot | `a_cut_through_after_the_side_turn_still_convicts_the_part` | red / green |\n\nThe lattice multiplication overflow guard cannot trigger after both axes pass the 4096-cell limit.\nThe maximum product fits both 32-bit and 64-bit `usize`.\nNo artificial oversized allocation was used to test that branch.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed on the first run.\nThe gate completed three steps with zero failures in 6.2 minutes.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nNo source changed after the gate.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nNo `.nc` or `.cl` golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nWindows, macOS, the full release gate, heavy tests, and pixel snapshots were not exercised.\n\nThe exact carry requires box stock with retained cut history.\nMesh stock, cylinder stock, raw grids, and edits that discard history keep the conservative carry from #874.\nThat fallback can still extend a face by one cell and fill a cavity.\n\nThe field engine keeps `FIELD_SIDE_CARRY_REFUSAL`.\nIts vertical cut records cannot prove material intervals along a new axis.\nRe-indexing its bricks alone cannot make that read safe.\nIssue #1805 permits this named refusal when the reason is recorded.\n\nThe branch contains no screenshots, logs, or review evidence artifacts.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\nThe open PR checks found no overlapping files.\n\nChangelog: Preserve machined wall positions and cavities through side-on turns of box stock with retained cut history, and allow fixtures to contact those walls.\n\nFixes #1805\n",
